cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or its derived data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Heat, green and the vote: Berlin 2026"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible PostGIS, Google Earth Engine and Python pipeline relating summer land surface
  temperature, vegetation (NDVI) and access to everyday services to party-list results of the
  Berlin Abgeordnetenhaus election of 20 September 2026, across 2,542 polling-station districts.
  Postal votes are allocated to station districts, indicators are computed over residential land
  (dasymetric), and correlations follow an analysis plan fixed before the satellite data existed.
  Ecological and descriptive: results describe districts, not voters. Version 0.1 uses the
  preliminary election results.
authors:
